    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup, **Yordan Alvarez** (75.62) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.09) represent our highest-ceiling plays. **Yordan Alvarez** is primed for a massive output against the shaky 5.83 xERA of the opposing starter, and despite the lefty-on-lefty platoon disadvantage, his elite 0.425 xwOBA remains the cornerstone of our lineup. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from wind-assisted conditions and a strong platoon split, making him an essential start despite hitting low in the order. **Trea Turner** (70.06) and **Colt Keith** (69.13) also rank among our elite options; **Trea Turner** leverages an advantageous wind direction, while **Colt Keith** exploits a favorable matchup against Cecconi, who remains a target for us given his high-volume SB allowance.\n\nWe are navigating several complex platoon dynamics, most notably with **Christian Yelich** (53.20) and **Dillon Dingler** (48.44). **Christian Yelich** struggled to clear the \"Strong\" start threshold due to a difficult matchup against the lefty Imanaga, and **Dillon Dingler** faces a similar dynamic penalty that suppresses his raw output. The most difficult benching decision involved evaluating the remaining depth on our roster against **Casey Schmitt** (61.88), who ultimately earned the UTIL spot due to his +11% dynamic platoon edge and hitting in the #3 hole against Gallen. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Zac Veen** closely; the absence of **Lars Nootbaar** (IL) and the minor league assignment of **Zac Veen** continue to thin our utility options. All managers should remain alert for potential late lineup adjustments to the lineups of **Junior Caminero** and **Hyeseong Kim**, as both players sit near the lower end of our active floor.",
